The figure shown is a right circular cylinder with a radius of $r$ and height of $h$. A second right circular cylinder (not shown) has a volume that is $392$ times as large as the volume of the cylinder shown. Which of the following could represent the radius $R$, in terms of $r$, and the height $H$, in terms of $h$, of the second cylinder?', NULL, '{"A":"$R = 8r$ and $H = 7h$","B":"$R = 8r$ and $H = 49h$","C":"$R = 7r$ and $H = 8h$","D":"$R = 49r$ and $H = 8h$"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', '[{"type":"description","content":"Figure: A right circular cylinder with radius $r$ and height $h$."}]'::jsonb, '{"corpus":"official-cb","file":"area-and-volume.ndjson"}'::jsonb);
