A tree had a height of $6$ feet when it was planted. The equation above can be used to find how many years $n$ it took the tree to reach a height of $14$ feet. Which of the following is the best interpretation of the number $2$ in this context?', NULL, '{"A":"The number of years it took the tree to double its height","B":"The average number of feet that the tree grew per year","C":"The height, in feet, of the tree when the tree was $1$ year old","D":"The average number of years it takes similar trees to grow $14$ feet"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', NULL, '{"corpus":"official-cb","file":"linear-equations-in-one-variable.ndjson"}'::jsonb);
INSERT INTO public.cb_questions (id, section, domain, cb_skill, difficulty, stem, passage, options, correct_answer, explanation, item_type, assets, source_ref)
VALUES ('7a5a74a6', 'M', 'Algebra', 'Linear equations in one variable', 'Medium', '$3(2x - 6) - 11 = 4(x - 3) + 6$
If $x$ is the solution to the equation above, what is the value of $x - 3$?', NULL, '{"A":"$\\frac{23}{2}$","B":"$\\frac{17}{2}$","C":"$\\frac{15}{2}$","D":"$-\\frac{15}{2}$"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', NULL, '{"corpus":"official-cb","file":"linear-equations-in-one-variable.ndjson"}'::jsonb);
INSERT INTO public.cb_questions (id, section, domain, cb_skill, difficulty, stem, passage, options, correct_answer, explanation, item_type, assets, source_ref)
VALUES ('9d4270fe', 'M', 'Algebra', 'Linear equations in one variable', 'Medium', 'A company that creates and sells tape dispensers calculates its monthly profit, in dollars, by subtracting its fixed monthly costs, in dollars, from its monthly sales revenue, in dollars. The equation $15{,}000 = 2.00x - 4{,}500$ represents this situation for a month where $x$ tape dispensers are created and sold. Which statement is the best interpretation of $2.00x$ in this context?', NULL, '{"A":"The monthly sales revenue, in dollars, from selling $x$ tape dispensers","B":"The monthly sales revenue, in dollars, from each tape dispenser sold","C":"The monthly cost, in dollars, of creating each tape dispenser","D":"The monthly cost, in dollars, of creating $x$ tape dispensers"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', NULL, '{"corpus":"official-cb","file":"linear-equations-in-one-variable.ndjson"}'::jsonb);
INSERT INTO public.cb_questions (id, section, domain, cb_skill, difficulty, stem, passage, options, correct_answer, explanation, item_type, assets, source_ref)
VALUES ('628300a9', 'M', 'Algebra', 'Linear equations in one variable', 'Hard', 'A science teacher is preparing the $5$ stations of a science laboratory. Each station will have either Experiment A materials or Experiment B materials, but not both. Experiment A requires $6$ teaspoons of salt, and Experiment B requires $4$ teaspoons of salt. If $x$ is the number of stations that will be set up for Experiment A and the remaining stations will be set up for Experiment B, which of the following expressions represents the total number of teaspoons of salt required?', NULL, '{"A":"$5x$","B":"$10x$","C":"$2x + 20$","D":"$10x + 20$"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', NULL, '{"corpus":"official-cb","file":"linear-equations-in-one-variable.ndjson"}'::jsonb);
