VALUES ('6daf8d70', 'M', 'Algebra', 'Linear inequalities in one or two variables', 'Medium', 'A homeowner wants to plant azaleas and boxwoods in a garden. The homeowner can plant at most 164 plants total. The number of azaleas must be no more than 3 times the number of boxwoods. Which system of inequalities represents this situation, where $a$ is the number of azaleas and $b$ is the number of boxwoods?', NULL, '{"A":"$a + b \\le 164$ and $a \\le 3b$","B":"$a + b \\ge 164$ and $a \\le 3b$","C":"$a + b \\le 164$ and $a \\ge 3b$","D":"$a + b \\ge 164$ and $a \\ge 3b$"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', NULL, '{"corpus":"official-cb","file":"linear-inequalities-in-one-or-two-variables.ndjson"}'::jsonb);
