VALUES ('aa95fb33', 'M', 'Advanced Math', 'Nonlinear Functions', 'Medium', '[Graph: The graph of the rational function $f$ is shown, where $y = f(x)$ and $x \ge 0$. The curve starts high near $x = 0$, decreases steeply, and approaches a horizontal asymptote near $y = 1$ as $x$ increases. It passes through approximately $(3, 3)$.]

The graph of the rational function $f$ is shown, where $y = f(x)$ and $x \ge 0$. Which of the following is the graph of $y = f(x) + 5$, where $x \ge 0$?', NULL, '{"A":"[Graph: A curve shifted down by $5$ units]","B":"[Graph: A curve compressed vertically]","C":"[Graph: A curve similar to the original but higher]","D":"[Graph: A curve shifted up by $5$ units, passing through approximately $(3, 8)$]"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', '[{"type":"description","content":"Graph: The graph of the rational function $f$ is shown, where $y = f(x)$ and $x \\ge 0$. The curve starts high near $x = 0$, decreases steeply, and approaches a horizontal asymptote near $y = 1$ as $x$ increases. It passes through approximately $(3, 3)$."},{"type":"description","content":"Graph: A curve shifted down by $5$ units"},{"type":"description","content":"Graph: A curve compressed vertically"},{"type":"description","content":"Graph: A curve similar to the original but higher"},{"type":"description","content":"Graph: A curve shifted up by $5$ units, passing through approximately $(3, 8)$"}]'::jsonb, '{"corpus":"official-cb","file":"nonlinear-functions.ndjson"}'::jsonb);
