The graph shows the height $y$, in feet, above the water of a diver $x$ seconds after the diver left the diving board. Which of the following is the best interpretation of the $x$-intercept of the graph?', NULL, '{"A":"The diver hit the water about $1.6$ seconds after leaving the diving board.","B":"The diver was about $1.6$ feet above the water when the diver left the diving board.","C":"The diver hit the water about $10$ seconds after leaving the diving board.","D":"The diver was about $10$ feet above the water when the diver left the diving board."}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', '[{"type":"description","content":"Graph: The graph shows the height $y$, in feet, above the water of a diver $x$ seconds after the diver left the diving board. The curve starts at approximately $(0, 10)$, rises to a maximum near $(0.6, 11)$, then descends and crosses the $x$-axis at approximately $(1.6, 0)$."}]'::jsonb, '{"corpus":"official-cb","file":"nonlinear-functions.ndjson"}'::jsonb);
