VALUES ('f2d60b99', 'M', 'Advanced Math', 'Nonlinear Functions', 'Hard', 'The function $f(x) = \frac{1}{9}(x - 7)^2 + 3$ gives a metal ball''s height above the ground $f(x)$, in inches, $x$ seconds after it started moving on a track, where $0 \le x \le 10$. Which of the following is the best interpretation of the vertex of the graph of $y = f(x)$ in the $xy$-plane?', NULL, '{"A":"The metal ball''s minimum height was $3$ inches above the ground.","B":"The metal ball''s minimum height was $7$ inches above the ground.","C":"The metal ball''s height was $3$ inches above the ground when it started moving.","D":"The metal ball''s height was $7$ inches above the ground when it started moving."}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', NULL, '{"corpus":"official-cb","file":"nonlinear-functions.ndjson"}'::jsonb);
